    "body": "Check of upstream/main: bcf2d132ada2ccdb362648a2e37d5138996e7836.\n\nThe main file commands have implementations. Do not implement them again.\n\n- PR #1438, merge f84059c97ca87cfecfc47f0e93f5f150b96630b8, added downloads for Save, Save As, and Post. See `crates/ui/src/state_browser.rs` and `crates/ui/src/browser_files.rs`. The structural tests in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/browser_files.rs` check the download data and the refusal state.\n- PR #1314, merge f2b42e3d301c9b7f24e78e5e4138904d5250a52e, added the model and project picker. See `crates/ui/src/file_pick.rs`, `crates/ui/src/state_picked.rs`, and `crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell_web.rs`. Both merge commits are ancestors of the checked upstream/main.\n- The PR #1314 record says that the wasm release build and page check passed. The user checked Chrome and Brave. The user then checked the Safari fix at 2026-11-14 01:10Z, build 32c66876 (the same tree as 0dd7eebc). In Safari, File > Model loaded simple.step, File > Open loaded simple.camproj, and the size limit refused the large file. The manager also confirms the browser check of Open, Open Model, and Save. I did not repeat these browser checks.\n\nSome acceptance conditions remain:\n\n1. `RELEASE_NOTES.md:177` and `RELEASE_NOTES.md:215` still say that the file picker is owed. The issue asks for removal of this known issue.\n2. Unsupported menu commands are refused after a click, but are not disabled with a reason before the click. In `crates/ui/src/egui_app/theme_drop.rs`, every theme row is live, including Browse. In `crates/ui/src/egui_app/fixture_menu.rs`, every row with a command has a click response and live text. This includes Import fixture and the two fixture library commands. `browser_files::refusal` refuses these commands, but the menus do not use that result. The issue asks for disabled menu items and buttons, with a reason.\n\nI did not claim the issue or change code. The UI rules require structural checks of the disabled state in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/structural.rs`. Open PR #1639 changes that file. The manager's instruction says to stop if the remaining fix must change a file in PR #1639. Work stops for that overlap. No labels were changed. No worktree or PR was created. No tests, mutation checks, or gate were run. No approval prompt was raised.\n",
